speechtext:
My memory
may be at fault in the matter; but, if so, the fact gives greater emphasis to the view I hold. My hon. friend from Kings (Mr. Hughes) has referred to some words of mine to the effect that I should be sorry that any province should feel that it had a grievance on account of its representation. I should be sorry that in matters of representation or any other matters a province should feel that it was .aggrieved in any way by anything done or left undone by this Parliament. It is of the very essence of our Constitution that we should endeavour to have all provinces fairly represented, and the views of .all provinces accepted in this' Parliament in so far as we can attain that end. It may be that the condition I have referred to was in the report as stated by the Prime Minister; but I am certain that the hon. member for Pictou suggested that the amendment to the British North America Act referred to should be sought; and this was include in the Bill as it went from this House to the Senate. The Bill as reported was in these words:
There shall be In the province of Prince Edward Island three electoral districts, defined as follows :	,
1.	The county of Kings shall form and constitute the electoral district of Kings, and shall return one member;
2 The county of Prince shall form and constitute the electoral district of Prince, and shall return one member;
3. The county of Queens shall form and constitute the electoral district of Queens, and shall return one member.
My impression still is that this was the provision of the Bill as reported by the committee, and that the following amendment was added on the suggestion of the
hon. member for Pictou:
Provided that if the British North America Act 1867, should be amended by the Parliament of the United Kingdom, in accordance with the address of both Houses of the Parliament of Canada in that behalf, passed at the present session, immediately upon the Act of the Parliament of the United Kingdom amending the said British North America Act, 1867, in accordance with such address, coming into force there shall be in the province of Prince Tainnd three electoral districts defined
as follows:
1.	The county of Kings shall form and constitute the electoral district of Kings and shall return one member;
2.	The county of Prince shall form and constitute the electoral district of Prince and shall return one member;
